From b8820679a6fdb8b308723f5a0dc3cc38b4c2f79b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:15:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] wxGUI/nviz: draw the 3D view in stereo

Ask the GL canvas for a stereo visual (WX_GL_STEREO) when "3D view in stereo"
is set in the Map Display settings, and use the mono visual when the display
does not offer one. In stereo, UpdateMap() draws the scene once per eye and
the decorations into each eye's back buffer, then swaps once. The north arrow,
scale bar and fringe are part of the scene and follow the eye's camera, the
legend and text images are 2D and are drawn the same in both eyes.

New settings next to the depth buffer: "3D view in stereo" (applies to 3D
views opened afterwards, the visual is chosen when the canvas is created) and
"3D view eye separation" in percent of the distance to the focus point.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
---
 gui/wxpython/core/settings.py        |   6 ++
 gui/wxpython/gui_core/preferences.py |  44 ++++++++++++
 gui/wxpython/nviz/mapwindow.py       | 101 ++++++++++++++++++---------
